target/
!target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/trading-bot
!target/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/release/copy-trading-bot
.env
portfolio_state.json
.git/
# Local dev worktrees (coord/ isolated branches). Each carries its own multi-GB
# target/ dir; without this the build context balloons to >10GB and the transfer
# stalls the deploy. Keep them out of the image build entirely.
wt/
dogfood-tmp/

# Nightly pg_dumps. NOT optional — this line is why prod survives a deploy.
#
# On 2026-07-13 these were still in the build context: 5.2 GB of dumps made the
# transfer 4.87 GB, and pushing that onto a disk with 134 MB free threw an I/O
# error mid-build, wedged the Docker daemon, and took prod down. The VM's ext4
# journal had already aborted the day before for the same underlying reason (the
# nightly dump filling the disk). The dumps are pure BUILD-IRRELEVANT payload —
# the image never reads them.
backups/

# Local Parquet archive (hot/cold split) — same story: bulk data the image never
# reads, and it grows without bound.
archive/
*.parquet
